Examples for gr-soarr
=====================

db_client_example.yaml
----------------------

Example key/counter database for the db_client block's local-file mode.
db_client answers inject_db's lookups (keyed by SCID and SPI) with the
matching entry's VCID, encryption key, authentication key, SDLS counter,
and VCID counter.

To use it in GNU Radio Companion, set the db_client block's parameters to:

    type      = 1
    yaml_path = <path to this file>

Each entry needs SCID and SPI; the other fields are:

    VCID                virtual channel the frame is sent on
    encryption_key      AES-256 key for sdls_encryption, 64 hex characters
    authentication_key  AES-256 key for sdls_authentication, 64 hex characters
    sdls_counter        starting SDLS counter (the IV sent in the SDLS header)
    vcid_counter        starting frame sequence number for the virtual channel
    key_state           informational only; stored, not used by any block

Counters are served, then incremented in memory for as long as the block
runs; the file itself is never written back.

Instead of the flat "entries" layout used here, entries may also be
nested by SCID, then SPI:

    entries:
      "341":
        "1": { VCID: 18, encryption_key: ..., authentication_key: ... }

If the file is missing, cannot be parsed, or contains no valid entry,
db_client logs an error and falls back to its built-in dummy entry.

The keys in this file are well-known test patterns. Never use them with
a real spacecraft.
